            <ArticleTitle>[Comparative analysis of the information value of electrocardiographic loading tests in relation to the characteristics of atherosclerotic lesions of the coronary arteries].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>54-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Diagnostic possibilities of various exercise tests (bicycle ergometry, the dipyridamole test, atrial electrostimulation) were demonstrated, as was a relationship between their sensitivity and the number of stenosed coronary arteries, the extent and level of obstruction, collateral circulation specificity and myocardial function.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
